  "text": "Black holes are regions of space -time where gravity is so strong that nothing, not even light, can escape. They form when massive stars collapse under their own weight after exhausting nuclear fuel. The boundary around a black hole called the event horizon marks the point of no return. Inside the horizon, all matter is crushed toward a singularity, a point of infinite density where known physics breaks down. Black holes are characterized mainly by mass, spin, and electric charge.",
